-- Passage rg8-context-clues-p02
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('3c77a14c-fb28-57cd-8796-83bf7b4046db', 'rg8-context-clues-p02', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-context-clues'), null,
        '6-8', $q$The Loose Wire$q$, $q$Ana Folau was the most meticulous member of the robotics team. She checked every screw twice, labeled every cable, and kept a notebook of every change the team made to the robot. Her teammates teased her about it, but they also asked her to inspect the robot before every match.

On the morning of the regional competition, though, it was Ana who felt flustered. Her hands shook, her words came out in the wrong order, and she dropped the same screwdriver three times. The team's robot had stopped responding during the practice round, and no one knew why.

"We have twelve minutes," said Marcus Delgado, the team captain. "We cannot rebuild the arm. We need to improvise."

Ana nodded. Without the spare part they had left at school, they would have to make do with whatever was in the toolbox. She traced the wires with one finger until she found the problem: a connector that had worked itself loose.

The fix was crude, nothing like the neat wiring Ana usually insisted on. A strip of tape and a zip tie held the connector in place. Still, when the match started, the arm lifted every block the drivers asked it to.

When the final buzzer sounded, the team had won by four points. The stands erupted. Marcus was jubilant, leaping and shouting until his voice cracked, and even quiet Ana let out a cheer.

Later, the captain of the rival team walked over. "Your robot was better today," she conceded, shaking Ana's hand. "We will see you at the state tournament."$q$, 'draft')
