   $q$Which meaning of "treacherous" is best supported by the examples in paragraph 2?$q$, $q$[{"text":"full of hidden dangers","is_correct":true},{"text":"deep and very cold","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"calm and easy to cross","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"crowded with many ships","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"surface-association"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$full of hidden dangers$q$, $q$The examples "hidden rocks, shifting sandbars, and sudden fog" that could "tear open the hull" show the waters were full of hidden dangers. Nothing in the paragraph mentions the water's depth or temperature.$q$, 'draft', 'dea1a239-7b14-599e-9914-0ddbc58f17f7')
