values
  ('e496b782-e052-59db-af81-9d49b3331d37', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-context-clues'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The author compares the waves in paragraph 3 to adding positive five and negative five. What does this comparison show about the meaning of "counteract"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Two matching forces join together to become stronger.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"One force is measured with numbers and math.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Two opposite forces work against each other and cancel out.","is_correct":true},{"text":"One force reacts later than the other one does.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Two opposite forces work against each other and cancel out.$q$, $q$Positive five plus negative five equals zero, just as opposite waves "cancel out," so counteract means to work against something and cancel its effect. The comparison uses math, but the word itself is not about measuring with numbers.$q$, 'draft', '1c44f6ff-cb9f-57e6-8e1d-3b3065baea3f')
