   $q$Ms. Varga explains what she means by "cohesive" in paragraph 2. A "cohesive" mural is one whose parts:$q$, $q$[{"text":"fit together into one unified picture","is_correct":true},{"text":"are painted in bright, bold colors","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-context-clue"},{"text":"are each painted by a different student","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"show many unrelated, separate ideas","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$fit together into one unified picture$q$, $q$Ms. Varga says the parts "have to fit together and feel like one picture, not twenty-six separate ones." Showing separate ideas is exactly what she says a cohesive mural should not do.$q$, 'draft', '337b6a72-8c9c-5cc9-bd7e-7d39ff42813c')
