   $q$According to the passage, what are the two ways trees cool a street?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They absorb heat from asphalt and release it slowly after sunset.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-subject"},{"text":"They grow deep roots that pull heat down into the soil.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They block the wind and keep the pavement from cracking.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"They shade the ground and release water vapor that carries heat away.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They shade the ground and release water vapor that carries heat away.$q$, $q$The second paragraph says leaves "block sunlight" and that trees "release water vapor" that carries heat away when it evaporates. Absorbing heat and releasing it after sunset is what the passage says asphalt does, not trees.$q$, 'draft', '4a9f1307-b21b-5181-b921-6c412b472af9')
