   $q$Which statement can be inferred from the passage but is NOT stated directly in it?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Keepers cleaned the lens and polished brass nearly every morning.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"stated-not-inferred"},{"text":"Many keeper families had to leave their stations once lights became automatic.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Most keepers disliked living so far from other families.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Many lamps in the 1800s burned whale oil and later kerosene.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"stated-not-inferred"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Many keeper families had to leave their stations once lights became automatic.$q$, $q$The passage says keepers "were no longer needed" and stations "were left empty," which suggests families moved away, though it never says so directly. The choices about cleaning and fuel are stated outright, and nothing in the text describes how keepers felt.$q$, 'draft', '71b51725-6704-547c-8957-ff13f000b1a2')
