   $q$Faith says Kenji is not "cheap" but "thrifty." What is the difference she is pointing out?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Both mean careful with money, but \"thrifty\" sounds wise and \"cheap\" sounds stingy.","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"Thrifty\" means spending a lot of money, while \"cheap\" means spending none.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-denotation"},{"text":"Both sound insulting, but \"thrifty\" is the more polite way to complain.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-connotation"},{"text":"\"Cheap\" is about money, while \"thrifty\" is about saving time on projects.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-denotation"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Both mean careful with money, but "thrifty" sounds wise and "cheap" sounds stingy.$q$, $q$The two words share a denotation, being careful with money, but "thrifty" has a positive connotation and "cheap" a negative one. Faith is defending Kenji, so she is not complaining about him at all.$q$, 'draft', '2d7f08c4-8dab-54c2-871c-7a3e1b97b79f')
