   $q$Mrs. Petrosyan's tomato vines "climbed their cages like eager kids on a jungle gym." What does this simile suggest about the vines?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They were growing upward quickly and with lots of energy.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They were small and struggling, like Darnell's pepper.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"They were planted in a playground near the garden.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"They were tangled and about to fall off their cages.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They were growing upward quickly and with lots of energy.$q$, $q$Eager kids scramble up a jungle gym fast, so the vines are growing up their cages vigorously. The passage contrasts the vines with Darnell's pale pepper, so they are not struggling.$q$, 'draft', '5aeb9ff3-6716-500d-8fb7-b2db9eb52faf')
