   $q$Darnell's mother calls him "stubborn," and Mrs. Petrosyan calls him "determined." Why does Darnell like "determined" better?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It means he is lazy, which he finds funny and true.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-denotation"},{"text":"It describes the same refusal to quit but makes it sound admirable.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It describes a completely different habit than \"stubborn\" does.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-shared-denotation"},{"text":"It sounds harsher, and he wants to seem tough to his mother.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reversed-connotation"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It describes the same refusal to quit but makes it sound admirable.$q$, $q$Both words describe someone who keeps going no matter what, but "determined" praises that quality while "stubborn" criticizes it. The words share a core meaning, so they do not describe different habits.$q$, 'draft', '5aeb9ff3-6716-500d-8fb7-b2db9eb52faf')
