   $q$Scientists describe the migration route as "a highway in the sky." What does this metaphor mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It is a paved road that was built for the butterflies.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"It is a well-traveled route that many monarchs follow.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It is a route that only one butterfly uses each year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It is a path where butterflies must avoid airplanes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It is a well-traveled route that many monarchs follow.$q$, $q$Like a busy highway, the route carries huge numbers of travelers along the same path every year. The passage says "millions" of monarchs make the trip, so it is not a route for one butterfly.$q$, 'draft', '89b4504f-6945-5d63-a6e0-b236c3d2ed1f')
