   $q$Why does the reader feel suspense when Coach says she will get the stopwatch bag herself?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The reader knows Coach is angry that Wren asked about her running stride.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-character"},{"text":"The reader knows the banner is in that room, so the surprise could be ruined.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The reader knows the stopwatch bag has been lost somewhere on the field.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The reader fears Coach will be hurt carrying a heavy bag across the field.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The reader knows the banner is in that room, so the surprise could be ruined.$q$, $q$Because the reader knows the banner is hidden in the equipment room, Coach's plan to go there threatens the surprise. Nothing suggests the bag is heavy or that Coach could be hurt.$q$, 'draft', '055b2607-5671-53ce-88c8-4e18850fa7f7')
