-- Passage rg8-literary-structure-pov-p02
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('0e291c57-6810-5448-99f8-37d7d5e29fb6', 'rg8-literary-structure-pov-p02', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-literary-structure-pov'), null,
        '6-8', $q$The Footbridge Over Miller Creek$q$, $q$I was built by a town in a single summer.
Twelve neighbors carried boards across the field.
They hammered until the moon came up.
And still I hold.

In autumn, children race across my back.
They count my planks out loud, one to forty.
They drop leaves on one side and run to the other
to watch them float away beneath me.
And still I hold.

In winter, the creek goes quiet under ice.
A woman walks her old dog across each morning.
She stops halfway and tells him the weather.
He never answers, but he listens.
And still I hold.

In spring, the water rises brown and fast.
It tugs at my posts and pulls at my nails.
For three nights, it roars and argues with me.
On the fourth morning, it gives up and goes home.
And still I hold.

Now a sign says a new bridge is coming,
one made of steel, wider and stronger than I am.
I do not mind. I have carried enough.
Let the new bridge learn the children's counting.
Let it hear the weather every morning.
Let it hold.$q$, 'draft')
