   $q$Who is the speaker of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The woman who walks her dog every morning","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-speaker-character"},{"text":"The wooden footbridge that crosses the creek","is_correct":true},{"text":"One of the children who counts the planks","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-speaker-character"},{"text":"The creek that rises fast in the spring","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-speaker-character"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The wooden footbridge that crosses the creek$q$, $q$The speaker says "I was built by a town" and "children race across my back," so the speaker is the bridge. The woman and the children are people the bridge describes, not the voice of the poem.$q$, 'draft', '0e291c57-6810-5448-99f8-37d7d5e29fb6')
