   $q$How are stanzas two through four organized?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Each stanza is told by a different speaker in the town.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-speaker-character"},{"text":"Each stanza describes the bridge during a different season.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Each stanza moves backward in time to an earlier year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-structure"},{"text":"Each stanza describes a different neighbor who built the bridge.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Each stanza describes the bridge during a different season.$q$, $q$Stanzas two, three and four begin "In autumn," "In winter," and "In spring," so they move through the seasons in order. The builders appear only in the first stanza.$q$, 'draft', '0e291c57-6810-5448-99f8-37d7d5e29fb6')
