   $q$What is the effect of ending the first four stanzas with "And still I hold"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It tells the reader that nothing ever changes near Miller Creek.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"It suggests the bridge is about to break during the spring flood.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-repetition-effect"},{"text":"It shows the bridge wants the town to replace it with a new one.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"It stresses that the bridge stays steady through every change around it.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It stresses that the bridge stays steady through every change around it.$q$, $q$The line repeats after the building, the children, the quiet winter and the flood, so the refrain shows the bridge enduring each change. Even after the flood "gives up," the bridge still holds, so the refrain does not signal breaking.$q$, 'draft', '0e291c57-6810-5448-99f8-37d7d5e29fb6')
