   $q$In the last stanza, the refrain becomes "Let it hold." What does this change show?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The bridge is warning that the steel bridge will fail.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The bridge is passing its job on to the new bridge.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The bridge is asking the creek to stop its flooding.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-referent"},{"text":"The bridge is refusing to let the town replace it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The bridge is passing its job on to the new bridge.$q$, $q$The speaker says "I do not mind. I have carried enough," and "it" refers to the new bridge, so the changed refrain hands the job over. The calm words show the bridge is not refusing or warning.$q$, 'draft', '0e291c57-6810-5448-99f8-37d7d5e29fb6')
