   $q$How does the structure of the final stanza signal the poem's turn?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It opens with \"Now\" instead of a season, shifting from past memories to the present.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It adds a fifth season, showing that the bridge has lasted longer than expected.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"It switches to a new speaker, letting the steel bridge answer the old one.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-speaker-character"},{"text":"It repeats the first stanza word for word, showing that nothing has changed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It opens with "Now" instead of a season, shifting from past memories to the present.$q$, $q$The earlier stanzas open with seasons, but this one opens with "Now" and the news of a new bridge, which turns the poem from memory to the present moment. The speaker is still the old bridge, not the steel one.$q$, 'draft', '0e291c57-6810-5448-99f8-37d7d5e29fb6')
