   $q$How does the ending connect the present and the flashback?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The judge hands back the yellow ribbon, closing the story with a second award.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Nadia admits she lost, showing she regrets the six weeks spent on the project.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"The younger student turns out to be Felix, so the story ends where it started.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The sticky notes from the flashback return, showing Nadia now values her failures.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The sticky notes from the flashback return, showing Nadia now values her failures.$q$, $q$The two notes, PROJECT CANCELED and Felix's tip, come from the flashback, and Nadia shares them to show it did not work "the first time." She won third place, and she shares the notes proudly, not with regret.$q$, 'draft', '5e04c179-a9a8-5a40-9c61-0e23e6174a3f')
