-- Passage rg8-literary-structure-pov-p08
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('5154a87c-f315-53d4-9481-7d758b9e0a2a', 'rg8-literary-structure-pov-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-literary-structure-pov'), null,
        '6-8', $q$The Red Kite: Two Tellings$q$, $q$Part One: Saturday in the Park

Amir and his grandmother, Nana Ruth, launched the red kite at ten in the morning. The wind was steady, and the kite climbed until it was a small red diamond above the soccer fields. At eleven, a gust snapped the string. Amir chased the kite across two fields and a parking lot, but it landed in the top of a tall oak behind the library. He sat on the curb, sure it was gone forever. At noon, a librarian named Mr. Baptiste came out with a long pole he used to change light bulbs. Ten minutes later, the kite was back in Amir's hands, with only one small tear.

Part Two: Nana Ruth's Letter

Dear Leila,

Your cousin Amir has a red kite with a patch on it now, and he says the patch is his favorite part. Let me tell you why. On Saturday the string snapped, and the kite ended up in an oak tree behind the library. Amir sat on the curb looking as if the world had ended. Then a kind librarian walked out carrying a pole meant for light bulbs, and he rescued it. When we got home, Amir glued a patch over the tear himself. He wrote the date on it in marker.

Love,
Nana Ruth$q$, 'draft')
