   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Cities are often warmer than nearby areas because dark surfaces store heat, plants are removed and buildings trap warm air. Light roofs and more trees can reduce the effect.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Plants pull water from the ground and release it through their leaves. As the water evaporates, it cools the air in the same way that sweat cools a runner.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Cities are miserable in summer, and planners have done a poor job of protecting the people who live there. Everyone should demand that their city build more parks.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Air conditioners, cars and machines release heat into city streets. This extra heat is the main reason city neighborhoods stay warm long after the sun sets.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Cities are often warmer than nearby areas because dark surfaces store heat, plants are removed and buildings trap warm air. Light roofs and more trees can reduce the effect.$q$, $q$The choice about dark surfaces, removed plants and trapped air states the causes and the solutions without adding opinions. The choice calling cities "miserable" adds judgments, such as "miserable" and "poor job," which do not belong in an objective summary.$q$, 'draft', '1bbb76c8-c8c1-560b-a8f2-7212f530f898')
