   $q$Which is the best objective summary of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Governments decided that every town should follow the sun more closely. Railroads then printed new timetables to match each town's local time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Towns once kept local time based on the sun. Because this confused train schedules, railroads created time zones, which spread to other areas of life and later became official.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Towns once kept local time based on the sun. The railroads unfairly forced their own system on everyone, and it was a mistake that people still live with today.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"includes-opinion"},{"text":"Railroad timetables listed departures in many local times. Passengers grew confused, and a traveler could miss a connection by several minutes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Towns once kept local time based on the sun. Because this confused train schedules, railroads created time zones, which spread to other areas of life and later became official.$q$, $q$The choice about railroads creating time zones covers the whole sequence from sun time to official time zones without judging it. The choice saying railroads "unfairly" forced their system adds opinions ("unfairly," "a mistake") that the passage never states.$q$, 'draft', 'c4166e12-f7da-5d4e-9707-3948244136e6')
