   $q$Why does the uncle most likely silence his alarm "on the first note"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He dislikes the song that his alarm plays each morning.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"He hopes the speaker will hear it and get up with him.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"He does not want to wake the others who are still asleep.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He is running late and has no time to let it ring.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He does not want to wake the others who are still asleep.$q$, $q$The poem compares the dark to "a sleeping baby," which suggests he is being careful to keep the house quiet. Nothing says he dislikes the song; the comparison is about quiet, not taste.$q$, 'draft', '07fb6fed-7705-5e89-8bcd-aa3f85115900')
