values
  ('20b8cb5e-ae7b-5395-a354-fd7dda50666c', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-story-details-inference'), null, 'hard',
   $q$In the final paragraph, Tamsin still counts her acorns twice before planting some. What does this detail suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She has decided that counting is a waste of her time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"She no longer trusts Odo to bury acorns on the hill.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"She regrets planting acorns and wants to keep them all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"She has kept her careful habit while adding a new one.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She has kept her careful habit while adding a new one.$q$, $q$She counts "twice," just as she did at the start, and then plants ten acorns, so she combines her old habit with Odo's way. If she thought counting was a waste, she would have stopped doing it.$q$, 'draft', '391e7083-ed94-521f-a6b6-1693679227c9')
