   $q$How is paragraph 4 structured?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It presents an opposing view, admits it is fair, and then answers it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It offers a new reason that builds on the reason in paragraph 3.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-counterclaim"},{"text":"It lists the activities students already do after the school day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"It tells a personal story about the writer's broken backpack.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-paragraphs"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It presents an opposing view, admits it is fair, and then answers it.$q$, $q$The paragraph opens with "Some people argue," grants that "That concern is fair," and responds with "However." The list of sports and clubs is only part of the concession, not the whole paragraph's structure.$q$, 'draft', '21104bb5-f87b-544b-8336-21203666d096')
