   $q$Which statement would NOT belong in an objective summary of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The speaker crosses the finish line after all the other runners.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"objective-detail"},{"text":"The speaker remembers advice from Coach about what the race means.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"objective-detail"},{"text":"The speaker falls behind the other runners early in the race.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"objective-detail"},{"text":"The speaker should feel prouder than the winner, who did not struggle.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The speaker should feel prouder than the winner, who did not struggle.$q$, $q$An objective summary leaves out opinions, and saying the speaker "should" feel prouder than the winner is a judgment the poem never makes. The other three statements report events from the poem.$q$, 'draft', '101762e6-c650-57d3-aaf8-72335aace1a3')
