   $q$Which statement best expresses a theme of the story?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Young children should not be allowed to paint public murals.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Art made together can mean more than a perfect design.","is_correct":true},{"text":"A mural needs a full month of planning to succeed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Bright colors make any street feel more welcoming.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Art made together can mean more than a perfect design.$q$, $q$Keoni keeps the neighbors' imperfect work, and by the end he likes Amara's lopsided sun best. The story values Amara's part, so it does not suggest children should be kept out.$q$, 'draft', '610b96a2-00a0-566e-ae29-cd3828380abe')
