   $q$The root tele means "far," and graph means "write." What does "telegraph" mean in the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A chart that shows how far messages have traveled","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-sense-of-root"},{"text":"A horse and rider who deliver letters to towns","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-detail"},{"text":"A machine that prints pictures of faraway places","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal"},{"text":"A system for sending written messages over long distances","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A system for sending written messages over long distances$q$, $q$Tele plus graph means "far writing," and the passage explains that the telegraph carried messages along wires so they arrived in minutes. A horse and rider is what the telegraph replaced, not what the word means.$q$, 'draft', '8ee376fd-defe-5022-ac55-4ea657844dfe')
