   $q$The prefix pre- means "before," and the root dict means "say." What does "predict" mean in the first paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Shout loudly at the players on the field","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-first-root"},{"text":"Remember exactly what happened earlier","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-time-direction"},{"text":"Block the ball with both of her hands","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"Tell what will happen before it happens","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Tell what will happen before it happens$q$, $q$Pre plus dict means "say before," so the goalkeeper seemed to know where each shot would go before it was taken. Remembering looks back in time, while pre points forward.$q$, 'draft', '9e7ac8f4-6e05-5e57-bdee-e604ea847a07')
